IMPORT prelude

-- Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1941 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL), not the daydate library. The Act fixes no
-- period of its own. The dates that matter are commencement dates, all taken from the compilation table of the
-- deposited text:
--   - the Act itself: 24 October 1942 (s 1 and Gazette 23 Oct 1942 p 995);
--   - the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions (Asbestos Diseases)) Act 2002: 21 March 2002 (its s 2);
--   - the Civil Liability Amendment (Provisional Damages for Dust Diseases) Act 2024 Part 3: 1 December 2024
--     (s 2(1)(d) and SL 2024/238 cl 2);
--   - the Limitation Legislation Amendment and Repeal Act 2005: 15 November 2005 (its s 2(1)), the "commencement day"
--     of its savings provision s 15(4), printed in the notes (finding 4).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1941`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- TRUE when the first date is strictly after the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls after` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

`the commencement of this Act` MEANS `the calendar date` 24 10 1942
`the commencement of the Asbestos Diseases Act 2002` MEANS `the calendar date` 21 3 2002
`the commencement of Part 3 of the Dust Diseases Act 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 12 2024
`the 2005 limitation commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 11 2005
